{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.yekutieli_levi_unification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.yekutieli_levi_unification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.NoZeroSMulDivisors.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_regular_of_sheet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_regular_of_sheet","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L122-L130","doc":"**Branch B (regular side).** If the Levi form degenerates (the core flattens\ninto a sheet), the leading NS obstruction on `Σ` vanishes — categorically\nNS-regular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_nondegenerate_of_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_nondegenerate_of_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L114-L120","doc":"**Branch A (blow-up side).** A surviving obstruction forces the Levi form to\nbe non-degenerate at `p` (discrete cores, no sheet). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_obstruction_iff_levi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.ns_obstruction_iff_levi","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L102-L112","doc":"**The Yekutieli–Levi unification.** With nontrivial linking, the leading NS\nobstruction on `Σ` is nonzero **iff** the Levi form is non-degenerate at `p`\n— the categorical face of the Levi dichotomy. Derived from `kappa_def`,\n`smul_ne_zero_iff`, and the two geometric equivalences (c)/(d). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.eulerResidue_iff_localCohom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.eulerResidue_iff_localCohom","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**Steps (c)/(e):** the Euler residue is nonzero ⟺ the local cohomology at\n`p` is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.localCohom_iff_levi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.localCohom_iff_levi","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L95-L95","doc":"**Step (d):** local cohomology nonvanishing ⟺ Levi non-degeneracy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.leviNonDegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.leviNonDegenerate","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L93-L93","doc":"\"`λ∥(p) > 0 ∧ λ⊥(p) > 0`\": the Levi form is non-degenerate at `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.localCohomNonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.localCohomNonzero","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L91-L91","doc":"\"`H¹_{𝔪_p}(A) ≠ 0`\": the local cohomology at `p` is nonzero (both cores\ncarry local sections; no sheet). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.kappa_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.kappa_def","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L88-L88","doc":"**Step (e):** the leading obstruction is the linking multiple of the\nEuler residue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.kappaLeading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.kappaLeading","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The leading NS obstruction `κ_n|_Σ = lk · e(ξ)|_Σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.linking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.linking","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The linking number `lk(ϱ₁, ϱ₂)` of the anti-parallel pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.eulerResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.eulerResidue","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The Euler residue `e(ξ)|_Σ ∈ H²(Σ, 𝓑)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstructionLeviData","kind":"class","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/yekutieli_levi_unification.lean#L70-L98","doc":"Local-cohomology / Levi / Euler-residue data at a collision point `p ∈ Σ`,\nfrom `ns-obstruction-tower` steps (c)–(e).\n\n`M` is the coefficient group `H²(Σ, 𝓑)` (torsion-free at leading order);\n`linking : ℤ` is `lk(ϱ₁, ϱ₂)`; the leading obstruction is the integer\nmultiple `kappaLeading = linking • eulerResidue`. The two `Prop` fields are\nthe geometric equivalences the manuscript proves (c)/(d): they carry the\nreal content, so the class is non-degenerate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}